-- title:
--   Local–global compatibility of the idelic Artin map at w
-- statement:
--   Let $F/E$ be a finite Galois extension of number fields whose group $G=(F\simeq_E F)$ is generated by an element $s$ of finite order (every $g\in G$ lies in `Subgroup.zpowers s`) and is commutative, and let $D$ be a Galois descent datum for the adeles of $F$: a homomorphism $G\to\operatorname{RingAut}(\mathbb A_F)$ by continuous automorphisms compatible with $F\to\mathbb A_F$. Fix actions of $G$ on $\mathbb A_F^\times$ and on $F^\times$ agreeing with $D$ and with the field action respectively, a morphism $j$ of $\mathbb Z$-linear $G$-representations $F^\times\to\mathbb A_F^\times$ induced by the principal-idele map, a prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_E$ and a prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_F$ above it, and a morphism $\mathrm{pr}$ from $\mathbb A_F^\times$ restricted to the decomposition subgroup $D_w\le G$ of the valuation subring of $w$ to $(F_w)^\times$, given by the $w$-coordinate `finPart w`. Let $\mathfrak f\neq 0$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ divisible by $v^{\,e}$ with $e$ the admissible exponent for the degree $[F:E]$ at every $v$ with nontrivial inertia in $F$, and let $r\colon\mathbb A_E^\times\to G$ be a homomorphism that kills the principal ideles, has kernel the principal ideles times the image of the idelic norm of `genuineBaseChange E F`, is surjective, and on ideles $1$-adjusted at $\mathfrak f$ (unit valuation and congruence to $1$ to the exact order of $\mathfrak f$ at each prime dividing $\mathfrak f$, positive at each real embedding) equals $\prod^{\mathrm f}_{v}\operatorname{Frob}_v^{\operatorname{ord}_v}$ with the arithmetic Artin Frobenius. Let $a\in E^\times$ and let $x\in\mathbb A_E^\times$ have trivial infinite part and trivial component at every finite place other than $v$, with $w$-free $v$-component the image of $a$ in $(E_v)^\times$. Assume the carry function of $(s,a)$, namely $(g,h)\mapsto a$ if $\operatorname{ord}(s)\le \mathrm{cyclicLog}(g)+\mathrm{cyclicLog}(h)$ and $0$ otherwise, with $a$ taken in $F^\times$, is a $2$-cocycle. On the local side, fix a prime $q$, a finite extension $L'$ of $\mathbb Q_q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q_q}$ with a $D_w$-action on $L'$ and on $(L')^\times$, a ring isomorphism $\Phi\colon F_w\cong L'$, hypotheses that $D_w$ fixes the $\mathbb Q_q$-scalars, acts on units compatibly, and that $\Phi$ is equivariant, a finite subextension $K_0$ with $K_0\le L'$ and $K_0$ the $D_w$-fixed field of $L'$, a representation morphism $\theta\colon (L')^\times\to (F_w)^\times$ induced by $\Phi^{-1}$, and a class $u'\in H^2(D_w,(L')^\times)$ that is a local fundamental class in the sense of [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60). Then there exist $n_w\in\mathbb Z$ and $i\in\mathbb N$ such that the image of the carry class in $H^2(G,F^\times)$ under $H^2(j)$ followed by restriction to $D_w$ and $H^2(\mathrm{pr})$ equals $n_w\cdot H^2(\theta)(u')$, $r(x)=s^i$, and $n_w/\#D_w$ and $i/\#G$ agree in $\mathbb Q/\mathbb Z$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility of the idelic Artin map read in invariant form: at the finite place $w$ the coordinate $n_w/\#D_w$ of the cyclic carry class of $(s,a)$ against the local fundamental class records $\chi_s(r(x))$, where $x$ is the idele concentrated at $v$ with component $a$; no unramifiedness is assumed. It feeds the cyclic-case assembly of the global reciprocity law, being used in [`M4aHerbrand.exists_forall_mem_zpowers_idelicArtinMap_single_of_isCyclic`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_forall_mem_zpowers_idelicArtinMap_single_of_isCyclic) and in [`M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_eq_zero_of_isCyclic`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_eq_zero_of_isCyclic).
